    { "text": "Not by spending 10x the time or effort, but by achieving 10x the leverage. This number is arbitrary — it's 2x, it's 10x, it's 100x. It all depends on the leverage points you can find.", "approx_timestamp": "5:19" },
    { "text": "Stop coding.", "approx_timestamp": "6:52" },
    { "text": "Your hands and your mind are no longer the best tool for the job of writing code, full stop.", "approx_timestamp": "7:19" },
    { "text": "But remember, you're an engineer, not a coder. The difference is massive.", "approx_timestamp": "7:57" },
    { "text": "To scale into this new phase two role, we need to allocate our engineering cycles to planning, reviewing, and creating closed loop structures.", "approx_timestamp": "8:55" },
    { "text": "Claude Code is not just writing code. It's calling tools. It's doing engineering work.", "approx_timestamp": "12:48" },
    { "text": "The new element that transforms the big three of AI coding to Agentic Coding is prompts that can reliably execute long chains of tools.", "approx_timestamp": "13:49" },
    { "text": "It's not a question of new. It's a question of scale and performance.", "approx_timestamp": "14:27" },
    { "text": "Claude Code is the first Agentic Coding tool to properly combine three essential elements: a powerful language model that can reason when needed, the ability to consistently call long chains of tools, and the right agent architecture.", "approx_timestamp": "14:51" },
    { "text": "Reliable Agentic Coding at scale was not possible before Claude Code. Everything we do in TAC is built upon this core idea you can see right in this readme with just 35 lines.", "approx_timestamp": "16:24" },
    { "text": "Agentic coding is not about us writing code. It's about building systems that build systems on our behalf.", "approx_timestamp": "20:34" },
    { "text": "To become an irreplaceable engineer, you will replace yourself.", "approx_timestamp": "20:47" },
    { "text": "10 minutes of your work is equivalent to 60 minutes or more of another engineer's work.", "approx_timestamp": "21:44" }
