    { "q": "What makes Claude Code 'programmable,' and why does that matter?", "a": "It runs in the terminal, so any language with terminal access can invoke it (claude -p with a prompt string). That turns the agent into a callable component you can embed across the software development lifecycle — even in environments where you're not present." },
    { "q": "Where do your engineering cycles go in phase 2?", "a": "Planning, reviewing, and creating closed-loop structures." },
