The standards pass found two real design-system violations: chapter-local layout styles and hard-coded SVG/palette values. I’m correcting them by moving the missing values into shared tokens, replacing inline layout with named classes, and tokenizing diagram presentation. The review’s performance note is also easy to address, so I’ll gate progress updates through animation frames.
